From e14eb464a18e8ea11e98fa2ea54bbc00bca92bbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:36:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: skip the items it marked bad when scumming in Lunal
 mode

The Lunal mode take routine works out for each visible item whether it
is worth a detour ("item_bad"), noting the ones it wants, but never read
the result: every item that passed the line-of-sight and stair-distance
tests became a target, including daggers and other things it meant to
leave. Skip the items marked bad.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#73.

(cherry picked from commit 45423c1c8d99bc7846dc8503fa0a2be0e5c7e149)
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-take.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
index 9c2baf06a..a2523f6e2 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-take.c
@@ -838,6 +838,10 @@ bool borg_flow_take_lunal(bool viewable, int nearness)
             }
         }
 
+        /* Skip items the Borg does not want */
+        if (item_bad)
+            continue;
+
         /* Get the grid */
         ag = &borg_grids[y][x];
 
-- 
2.53.0

